{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-4-6", "id": "msg_vrtx_01L8oRvcNH6kAj4AaGQVAUuA", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_vrtx_011n8c2KkeeF6q28u7qvp5fq", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/private/var/folders/3v/16m6pn090hl4d60grm1057ww0000gn/T/agent-eval/enhance-opt-iter-2/cases/case-003-short-proportionate/target-skill/SKILL.md", "content": "---\nname: \"text:count\"\ndescription: \"Count words, lines, and characters in a file. Use when the user asks to count words, get line counts, check file length, or measure text size. Do NOT use for code analysis, complexity metrics, or content summarization.\"\nargument-hint: \"<file-path>\"\nuser-invocable: true\n---\n\n# Word Counter\n\nCount words, lines, and characters in the specified file.\n\nRead the file at the provided path. Count:\n- **Lines**: split by newline\n- **Words**: split by whitespace (consecutive whitespace counts as one delimiter)\n- **Characters**: total length including whitespace\n\nIf the file is binary or unreadable, tell the user the file cannot be counted as text rather than reporting garbled numbers.\n\nReport the counts in this exact format:\n\n```\n**File**: `<path>`\n- Lines: <n>\n- Words: <n>\n- Characters: <n>\n```\n\nExample for a 3-line README:\n\n```\n**File**: `README.md`\n- Lines: 3\n- Words: 12\n- Characters: 87\n```\n\nIf the file does not exist, tell the user.\n"}}], "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3350, "cache_read_input_tokens": 42157, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 3350, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 8}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "41599ecf-e801-4cf0-a93d-b48fb8631778", "uuid": "ab6206a3-69df-4cd9-a6aa-df14d779ab8e", "timestamp": "2026-05-13T11:05:17.091Z"}
